       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA maximum of 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and other serious toxicity. Nothing in the patient details you gave (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function) would justify going that high.\n\nThis may be a typo. Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or PTSD:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n- **Panic disorder or social anxiety:** start at 25 mg once daily, then titrate to 50\u2013200 mg/day.\n\nCan you confirm the dose you want? For example, 50 mg, 60 mg, or 100 mg by mouth once daily. If you really do intend 600 mg, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy or psychiatry first. If you still want it entered after that, I can add a note to the order that the dose was verified."
      }
